      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, checking the p-trap underneath the sink is often the quickest DIY fix for a slow drain and bad smell. If the trap is loose or disconnected, reseating it will stop the smell immediately, but you must run a little water after to avoid air leaking into your house. Alternatively, a bidet-style plunger designed for sinks can sometimes dislodge a shallow blockage if you cover less than the entire basin edge and seal around the rim to create pressure. If those steps don't work despite checking for loose pipes and using a plunger, you are definitely ready to call a professional for an auger or camera inspection.",
